<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n50049" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vacca</span></b> , ae, f.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A town of Byzacene in Africa</i>, Auct. B. Afr.
			74.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A town of Numidia</i>, <i>called also
				Vaga</i>, now <i>Beja</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				29, 4</span></i>; <i><span class="en">47,
			1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">68, 3</span></i>;
				<i><span class="en">Sil.
				3, 259</span></i>. —Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vaccensis</span></b>  or <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vagensis</span></b> , e, adj., <i>of</i> or <i>pertaining to Vacca</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vagense oppidum,</span>”
				i. e. <i>Vaga</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					5, 4, 4, § 30</span></i>
			.— <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vaccenses</span></b> 
				(<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Vagen-</span></b> ),
				ĭum, m., <i>the inhabitants of Vacca</i>, <i><span class="en">Sall. J.
				66, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
